## Failure classes

Every run that ends with code 3 prints exactly one class line on standard error, for the first failure that ended it. The line starts with its group's prefix, then the class, a colon and a space, and then names what fails and the fix. Each further failure follows on a line of its own that holds its class, a colon, a space, what fails and the fix, with no group prefix.
{{with .Exits.failure_classes.setup}}
### Setup failures

{{.meaning}} Each line has the form `{{.prefix}}<class>: <detail>`.

| Class | Languages | Meaning | Fix |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
{{- range .classes}}
| `{{.class}}` | {{range $i, $l := .languages}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}`{{$l}}`{{end}} | {{.meaning}} | {{.fix}} |
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
